behaviour: An AlertManager payload missing the `entity_oddrn` label is silently accepted,
  persisted with a null `data_entity_oddrn`, and orphaned. The controller returns
  204 No Content with no warning. Operators relying on AlertManager's notification-success
  signal cannot detect this misconfiguration. STRENGTHENED batch P — the AlertManagerController#postAlerts
  sidecar PRIMARY-SOURCE at the method tier confirms the silent-orphan via the unconditional
  204 (`AlertManagerController.java:25 .map(o -> ResponseEntity.noContent().build())`
  — discards the inner signal entirely so callers cannot distinguish how many alerts
  were accepted, how many were orphaned, how many duplicated an existing OPEN alert).
  Plus the doc-side verbatim 2026-05-20: "[An alert submitted without this label]
  will not appear on any entity's page, and is effectively orphaned." The receiver
  is the ONLY path that produces this exact orphan shape — the in-platform ingestion
  path (`applyAlertActions` at AlertServiceImpl.java:222-227) uses the AlertActionResolver
  which does NOT permit a null data-entity-oddrn anchor.
